  "notes": "{蘇生|そせい} means resuscitation or revival — bringing someone or something back to life. Composed of {蘇|そ} (revive) + {生|せい} (life).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {心肺|しんぱい}{蘇生|そせい}: cardiopulmonary resuscitation (CPR)\n- {蘇生|そせい}{術|じゅつ}: resuscitation technique\n- {蘇生|そせい}する: to resuscitate, to revive\n- {蘇生|そせい}{措置|そち}: resuscitation measures\n\nUSAGE:\nMost commonly encountered in the medical compound {心肺|しんぱい}{蘇生|そせい} (CPR). Also used figuratively for the revival of economies, communities, or traditions (e.g., {地域|ちいき}の{蘇生|そせい} — revival of a region).\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {復活|ふっかつ}: revival, comeback (broader, less medical)\n- {回復|かいふく}: recovery (from illness, downturn)\n- {蘇生|そせい}: specifically bringing back from death or near-death",
